 Running Prettier without `--cache` will delete the cache.
 
-Also, since the cache file is stored in `./node_modules/.cache/prettier/.prettier-cache`, so you can use `rm ./node_modules/.cache/prettier/.prettier-cache` to remove it manually.
+By default, the cache file is stored in `./node_modules/.cache/prettier/.prettier-cache`.
+Use `--cache-location` to specify a different cache file, for example to keep
+separate caches for different projects that share a `node_modules` directory.
+Relative paths are resolved from the current working directory.
+
+```bash
+prettier --write --cache --cache-location ./.prettiercache src
+```
+
+You can remove the cache manually by deleting the configured cache file.
 
 > Plugins version and implementation are not used as cache keys. We recommend that you delete the cache when updating plugins.
 
